# CR 704.5v: a Battle at zero or less defense goes to its owner's graveyard
# -- destroyZeroDefense, run right after assignBattleProtector in the same
# state-based-action pass. assignBattleProtector asks unconditionally for
# any Battle with no protector yet, so a queued answer is still needed even
# though destroyZeroDefense is about to send this one straight to the
# graveyard the very next statement -- CheckStateBasedActions asking before
# checking is what battle-protector-assigned-to-opponent's own comment means
# by "the Battle would die to zero defense before this scenario ever got to
# observe its protector": the assignment still happens, there is just
# nothing left afterward for expect.state to show it on. Move only grants a
# Battle's printed starting defense on a real zone change
# (cast-a-battle-spell-resolves-to-battlefield is that case); this Battle is
# placed directly by setup.state (Game.NewCard), which sets exactly what the
# fixture says and nothing more, so with no DEFENSE counters written here it
# already reads zero.
queue battleprotector ai
startturn human
